## Mailpit Email Capture

Mailpit is the live test site's email sink. Messages are captured locally and are not delivered to real recipients.

### Runtime And Routing

- WordPress mail on `mirror-help.arrayhash.com` is routed through the active WP Mail SMTP plugin to `127.0.0.1:1025` using the Other SMTP mailer, no encryption, Auto TLS off, and SMTP authentication off.
- Mailpit SMTP listens on `127.0.0.1:1025`; its web UI and API listen on `127.0.0.1:8025`. Both listeners are intentionally loopback-only.
- The human web UI is `https://mailpit.arrayhash.com`. Caddy provides HTTPS, reverse proxying, security headers, and HTTP Basic Authentication. Do not store its credentials in the repository.
- The Caddy site file is `/home/server-manager/caddy/arrayhash__mailpit.arrayhash.com.caddy`.
- Mailpit runs as the unprivileged `mailpit` system user from `/usr/local/bin/mailpit`. Its systemd unit is `/etc/systemd/system/mailpit.service`.
- Captured mail persists in `/var/lib/mailpit/mailpit.db`. Retention is capped at 1,000 messages and 30 days.

### Agent Workflow

- Codex, Claude, and other on-server agents should use `/usr/local/bin/mailpit-agent`. It talks to the localhost API without public credentials and returns stable JSON.
- Useful commands: `mailpit-agent status`, `mailpit-agent list [limit]`, `mailpit-agent latest-id`, `mailpit-agent latest`, `mailpit-agent show <id|latest>`, `mailpit-agent text <id|latest>`, and `mailpit-agent html <id|latest>`.
- For a false-positive-safe test, save the current ID before triggering the email, then wait for a message newer than that ID:

```bash
previous_id="$(mailpit-agent latest-id 2>/dev/null || true)"
# Trigger the WordPress action that should send mail.
mailpit-agent wait-new "${previous_id:-none}" 30 "expected subject text"
```

- `wait-new` accepts a previous ID (or `none`), a timeout from 1 through 3,600 seconds, and an optional case-insensitive subject substring. It exits `124` on timeout.
- Direct local API access is available at `http://127.0.0.1:8025/api/v1/`; for example, `curl -fsS http://127.0.0.1:8025/api/v1/info | jq`.

### Operations And Troubleshooting

- Service checks: `systemctl status mailpit`, `systemctl is-enabled mailpit`, and `journalctl -u mailpit --since today`.
- After changing the Mailpit unit, run `systemctl daemon-reload` and `systemctl restart mailpit`, then verify with `mailpit-agent status`.
- After changing the Caddy site, run `caddy validate --config /etc/caddy/Caddyfile` before `systemctl reload caddy`.
- A healthy public endpoint returns `401` without HTTP Basic Authentication and `200` after authentication. A healthy local API returns JSON from `/api/v1/info`.
- Every WP-CLI email test in this workspace must use the documented WordPress path and `--allow-root`.
- Never expose ports `1025` or `8025`, commit the public UI credentials, or forward/release captured messages unless the user explicitly asks.

